    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Bloom is the long-awaited second album from Spratleys, arriving 27 years after their debut Pony and continuing the group’s distinctive line of eccentric psychedelic rock with strong pop instincts. Built around the Tim Smith–Jo Spratley legacy, it has been noted for sounding both unmistakably rooted in the Cardiacs-adjacent world and freshly vital, with intricate hooks, whimsical turns, and a densely musical, often euphoric energy.\n\nReleased on ATE Music, Bloom has been received as a remarkably fitting follow-up that preserves the band’s off-kilter charm while expanding its melodic palette. Reviews highlighted tracks such as “Hands To Why,” “Klog,” and “Nancy” for their invention and momentum, and the album’s significance lies in how confidently it revives one of British cult rock’s most singular voices after such a long absence.",
